From 3dd208071039a2abd4bb9be0b6c411b76a73906d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Albus <albus@example.com>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 00:06:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Scaffold ros2-essentials: layered images, profile-based
 cells, hand-eye calibration

Structure
  docker/base            thin: distro, CyclomeDDS, colcon, UID-matched user
  docker/base-gui        + X11/rviz/rqt, so headless modules skip ~1.5GB of Qt
  docker/base-cuda       CUDA devel + ROS (see version caveat in the file)
  docker/modules/*       ur, realsense, calibration, tools, perception

Module boundaries are compose profiles, and a machine's identity is the
COMPOSE_PROFILES line in cells/<hostname>.env. Same repo on every bench.

The calibration image inherits from base-gui rather than from the UR or
RealSense images because easy_handeye2 consumes TF only -- it never links
against either driver.

Calibration is split producer/consumer: the calib profile writes a .calib,
scripts/promote_calibration.py turns it into calibrations/<cell>/extrinsics.yaml,
and cell_description publishes that as static TF on every boot. Results are
committed, date-stamped, and never overwritten.

src/ros_zmq_bridge is the single node that speaks ROS on behalf of the CUDA
sidecars, keeping rclpy out of their dependency graphs.
